 1302:    // They use a standard, but not well known, way of accessing the fields of the nodes.
 1303:    //
 1304:    // An example of how to use these functions is:
 1305:    //   
 1306:    //    getNodalValues(L, &Node::compZCoord, zLAtNodes);
 1307:    // 
 1308:    // Where L is the level at which the field is to be interpolated. The field can be either
 1309:    // a double (depth), an array (u[nvrt]), or a function that depends on the level (Node::compZCoord(int k)). 
 1310:    // There are different versions of getNodalValues for each of these cases.
